Z||000003||Toddster||05-30-2001||03:53 PM||||If he is selling it for $4000 I would wager that there is more than just "minor" repair work to be done.<P>Ask the following:<BR>1) what tranny is it? The stock automatic is not up to the job without being rebuilt. Firstly, you will pull 3000 rpm at 65 miles per hour which means about 8 miles to the gallon and too much heat!<P>2) Make sure it has AT LEAST a 2 5/8 inch thick radiator with 4 rows of 3/8 inch cores. AT THE LEAST, I repeat, THE LEAST! Also check to make sure that the radiator caps are rated to 16 pounds or higher. The stock Fiero 13 lbs caps won't do.<P>3) ask if it has had overheating problems before. <P>4) how is the computer connected? Or is it a carburator unit? <P>5) Make sure the fan belt can be removed without taking the engine apart. Extra clearance is needed and some people simply don't go to the trouble to cut the body far enough away to do it.<P>6) Miles? Oil leaks?, Rust?<P>7) How is the gas getting to the engine? New Electric fuel pump? Where is it mounted? is it protected from heat? If not, the average ambient engine compartment temp of a basic v-6 is enough to cook it!! Make sure it is well protected.<P>8)Is the Alternator heat sheilded? Same reason.<P>9) what kind of exhaust does it have? Some people fail to realize that the stock v-6 muffler was designed to move 2.8 liters of air...only! You need increased flow to handle 5.7 liters.<P>10) Is all the wiring neat? And tucked behind heat sheilds?<P>11) All the "usual" questions about condition,  (ie, tires, brakes, etc.)<P>These are just the basics. But find out who did the installation and what kit was used for the conversion.<p>[This message has been edited by Toddster (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||SPDFREK||05-30-2001||04:07 PM||||one last thing you might want to check would be to see what condition the mounts are in. IE are they cracked, worn, or just not there at all. my friend bought a V8, and had to replace all mounts cause they were the original V6 mounts he thinks. anyway was not a fun job.||||reg||1
